* Example 08: the NMOS sink array, its gate vb pulsed from 0 to 1.0 V (4 ns
* period, four periods from 0.5 ns; the run averages the record's last three
* whole periods, 4.5 to 16.5 ns), its drain net out held at 1.8 V.
* run.sh writes tb_rcc.cir (the DSPF itself: the RC netlist, for rcc) from
* this file, filling in @PDK_ROOT@ and @NETLIST@ (the simulators do not expand
* environment variables in include paths).
* SKY130 typical models, as the PDK installs them for ngspice (Xyce reads them).
.param mc_mm_switch=0 mc_pr_switch=0
.include "@PDK_ROOT@/sky130A/libs.tech/ngspice/corners/tt.spice"
.include "@PDK_ROOT@/sky130A/libs.tech/ngspice/r+c/res_typical__cap_typical.spice"
.include "@NETLIST@"

* the block's ports in the order magic writes them: vb out vss
Vout out 0 1.8
Vvss vss 0 0
Vvb vb 0 PULSE(0 1.0 0.5n 0.2n 0.2n 1.8n 4n)
Xdut vb out vss sink
* reltol 1e-4, tighter than the simulators' default 1e-3; ngspice reads this
* line's reltol too
.options timeint reltol=1e-4
.tran 0.02n 16.5n
.end
